    "created_at": "2020-07-13T15:21:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-07-13T15:50:25Z",
    "body": "Basically, this PR is adding another \"incumbent-like thing\" that gets propagated in the same way as incumbent: namely, the active script. In particular, the active script's base URL is used for `import()`.\r\n\r\nSo the example `` setTimeout(eval, 0, 'import(`./example.mjs`)'); `` is about propagating the active script, not about propagating the incumbent. (The incumbent would come into play with an example like `setTimeout(eval, 0, 'postMessage(...)')`.)\r\n\r\nSo indeed, this is a bit more in @hiroshige-g's area. But, it will likely impact the bindings code, because it will need propagation through Web IDL callback conversion + calling in the same way incumbent currently does.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/comments/657623987/reactions",
